>Y2</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-62026144-U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>62026144</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1120143A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BANDAI CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA BANDAI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIKAWA YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIKAWA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A walking device similar in external appearance to a real insect and capable of behaving like a real insect. The walking device (1) comprises a trunk (2) and at least two each legs (31-36) disposed on each side of the trunk (2). Installed in the trunk (2) are a power source (6), and a plurality of gears (51-56) rotated by the power source (6). The legs (31-36) are embedded at their rear portions in the trunk (2) and attached to the centers of rotation of the gears (51-56) so that they can be rotated in the rotation direction of gear axes. The legs (31-36), which are bendable, are formed such that their bent state can be maintained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de marche d'apparence extérieure identique à celle d'un insecte réel, et capable de se comporter comme cet insecte. Ce dispositif (1) comprend un tronc (2) et au moins deux rangées de pattes (31-36) disposées de chaque côté dudit tronc (2). Une source d'alimentation (6) est installée sur le tronc (2), et une pluralité d'engrenages (51-56) sont entraînés en rotation par ladite source d'alimentation (6). Les pattes (31-36) sont emboîtées dans le tronc (6), au niveau de leur partie arrièr, et fixées aux centres de rotation des engrenages (51-56), de sorte qu'elles peuvent tourner dans le sens de rotation des axes d'engrenage. Ces pattes (31-36), qui peuvent se replier, sont formées de sorte que leur état replié peut être maintenu.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>